      "side": 1,
      "message": "My motivation for this comment was: we do implement `for_each_pkvm_mapping()`, and in particular we do use it in a similar case in `pkvm_age_gfn_range()` below, so I just wanted to clarify why we can\u0027t use it here.\n\n\u003e Retrieve the first mapping in the range on every iteration\n\nThat is clear from the code?\n\n\u003e which invalidates tree iterators.\n\n\"invalidates\" sounds a bit unclear to me in this context. Dropping mmu_lock just makes those iterators unsafe?\n\nHow about e.g.: \"We cannot safely use for_each_pkvm_mapping() for walking the range here, since mmu_lock may be dropped between iterations when yielding.\" ?",
